WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(applause)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:04.760
- So, the Pandemic really
changed family life this year.

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:07.440
Jessica, did you still
get to do any family trips

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:08.273
over the summer?

00:00:08.273 --> 00:00:09.106
Did y'all do anything?

00:00:09.106 --> 00:00:11.490
- We like,

00:00:11.490 --> 00:00:12.323
yes.

00:00:12.323 --> 00:00:14.540
We did two road trips,

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:17.793
which we've never done one before this.

00:00:18.670 --> 00:00:19.990
I don't even think Cash and I

00:00:19.990 --> 00:00:21.580
ever took a road trip

00:00:21.580 --> 00:00:23.840
prior to having kids.

00:00:23.840 --> 00:00:26.170
Yeah, we've never done this one before.

00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:27.796
And we, (laughs)

00:00:27.796 --> 00:00:28.629
- (laughs) Sounds like
it went smoothingly well.

00:00:28.629 --> 00:00:30.580
- Drove to Wyoming.

00:00:30.580 --> 00:00:32.303
Yeah, we drove to Wyoming.

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:36.260
We stopped in Zion.

00:00:36.260 --> 00:00:37.910
It was 110 degrees.

00:00:37.910 --> 00:00:39.760
We were driving my brother's RV.

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:40.850
He did let us borrow it.

00:00:40.850 --> 00:00:42.330
It did not have air conditioning.

00:00:42.330 --> 00:00:46.330
It was 110 with no air conditioning.

00:00:46.330 --> 00:00:48.010
Sharing a bed with our toddler,

00:00:48.010 --> 00:00:51.023
who has never slept
outside of a crib before.

00:00:52.669 --> 00:00:55.363
And all my kids got very vomitous,

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:59.270
carsick the entire time.

00:00:59.270 --> 00:01:03.060
And when we landed in Zion at 11:00 PM,

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:03.893
which would they,

00:01:03.893 --> 00:01:04.990
they were like,

00:01:04.990 --> 00:01:09.410
it's two hours past the time
anyone is allowed to pull in,

00:01:09.410 --> 00:01:10.850
because it's lights out,

00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:13.630
this, you know, RV, whatever.

00:01:13.630 --> 00:01:15.460
And we're like, okay well anyways,

00:01:15.460 --> 00:01:17.030
we have nowhere else to go.

00:01:17.030 --> 00:01:18.590
So we're just gonna go here

00:01:18.590 --> 00:01:20.580
and park the thing,

00:01:20.580 --> 00:01:22.800
and Cash backs in.

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:24.980
And everyone's just like hot,

00:01:24.980 --> 00:01:26.620
and they wanna get out,

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:27.590
and we're starving.

00:01:27.590 --> 00:01:29.640
We haven't eaten in 10 hours.

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:33.470
And right when I take the
baby out of his car seat,

00:01:33.470 --> 00:01:35.995
he vomits in my mouth and my eyes.

00:01:35.995 --> 00:01:36.828
(gasps)

00:01:36.828 --> 00:01:37.717
(Audience murmurs)

00:01:37.717 --> 00:01:41.350
And everyone in the RV goes "Eew!"

00:01:41.350 --> 00:01:42.790
including Cash,

00:01:42.790 --> 00:01:44.110
and run out.

00:01:44.110 --> 00:01:45.820
And so I'm blinded

00:01:46.728 --> 00:01:49.280
by warm acid vomit.
- (laughs) Oh my God.

00:01:49.280 --> 00:01:51.397
- And it's in my (mumbles)

00:01:51.397 --> 00:01:52.247
"Ah, guys! Guys!"

00:01:53.360 --> 00:01:54.949
And he's covered in it.

00:01:54.949 --> 00:01:55.782
(laughs)

00:01:55.782 --> 00:01:56.615
(Audience laughs)

00:01:56.615 --> 00:01:58.850
And so, I, it's like my mom mind,

00:01:58.850 --> 00:02:02.400
knows how to like take
off his clothes quickly,

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:05.580
'cause I didn't want him
like running around the,

00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:08.447
getting the vomit all over the RV obvie.

00:02:08.447 --> 00:02:09.280
(laughs)

00:02:09.280 --> 00:02:11.070
And I like wanted to keep it contained.

00:02:11.070 --> 00:02:16.070
And then this fool jumps out the RV,

00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:17.289
in his diaper,

00:02:17.289 --> 00:02:18.122
(laughs)

00:02:18.122 --> 00:02:20.050
and starts chasing frogs,

00:02:20.050 --> 00:02:24.540
like nasty, wild toads or frogs.

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:29.540
And this is like our first
time out of our house in,

00:02:29.870 --> 00:02:32.200
sitting in four and a half, five months.

00:02:32.200 --> 00:02:33.033
- Huh?

00:02:33.033 --> 00:02:34.950
- And then he starts going
to other people's camps!

00:02:34.950 --> 00:02:35.995
COVID camps!

00:02:35.995 --> 00:02:36.956
(Audience laughs)

00:02:36.956 --> 00:02:38.737
I'm like, the baby's gonna get COVID.

00:02:38.737 --> 00:02:40.780
And I'm like, still have
the vomit everywhere.

00:02:40.780 --> 00:02:42.470
I'm like, what is happening?

00:02:42.470 --> 00:02:44.283
So this is like my, our first night,

00:02:44.283 --> 00:02:46.080
on our first road--
- That's a movie.

00:02:46.080 --> 00:02:48.500
That's the greatest scene from a movie.

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:49.730
- It was the worst.

00:02:49.730 --> 00:02:51.210
It was my nightmare.

00:02:51.210 --> 00:02:53.310
It was my actual nightmare.

00:02:53.310 --> 00:02:55.890
But then somehow, three weeks later,

00:02:55.890 --> 00:02:57.381
I'm like, "Let's do it again".

00:02:57.381 --> 00:02:58.214
(laughs)

00:02:58.214 --> 00:02:59.670
And so we forgot,

00:02:59.670 --> 00:03:01.060
went up to Bend, Oregon,

00:03:01.060 --> 00:03:02.480
which was beautiful.

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:04.460
They have, you know, bicycles,

00:03:04.460 --> 00:03:06.690
and very nice there.

00:03:06.690 --> 00:03:09.450
But then we accidentally were driving,

00:03:09.450 --> 00:03:11.870
and this time we did a Sprinter van,

00:03:11.870 --> 00:03:14.910
and we accidentally drove the kids into

00:03:14.910 --> 00:03:18.370
a couple of the fires in Napa by accident.

00:03:18.370 --> 00:03:20.213
So that was, that was that.

00:03:20.213 --> 00:03:22.636
- (laughs) Oh my God.

00:03:22.636 --> 00:03:24.630
- (chuckles) Should we
like just feel like,

00:03:24.630 --> 00:03:26.623
we lost cell phone service.

00:03:27.650 --> 00:03:28.568
It was just a,

00:03:28.568 --> 00:03:29.809
it was a situation.

00:03:29.809 --> 00:03:30.985
It was a situation.
- Oh my God!

00:03:30.985 --> 00:03:34.201
- So yeah, my kids might
have PTSD from road trips.

00:03:34.201 --> 00:03:35.151
They may not ever (mumbles) (laughs)

00:03:35.151 --> 00:03:36.172
- They're gonna be like, "I'm out."

00:03:36.172 --> 00:03:38.126
- (laughs) They might be scarred for life.

00:03:38.126 --> 00:03:40.709
(upbeat music)

